  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce complete C/C++ packages. Offline installation follows author removal; independent unchanged C11/GMP and C++20 callers replay after moving each installed tree, giving four replay executions plus two setup executions per selection. The full API checks per-site constructors, normalization, repeated record fields, active variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards, rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Primitive-base nominal C/C++ acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete C and C++ packages from two authors. Independent C11/GMP and C++20 callers install offline after author removal and replay after physical relocation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. Original archives retain the embedded Lean runtime and native dependencies; receipts, caller/process records, tamper results and selected sources are retained. External compiler binaries are not retained. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
